                                        describes the information and specifications related to the
                                        temperature sensors on the SMS.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">This section
                                        describes the information and specifications related to the
                                        temperature sensors on the SMS.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Most motor faults
                                        will eventually result in high temperatures. These high
                                        temperatures can be an indication of the excessive friction
                                        within a motor or of OtoSense™ SMS is equipped with two
                                        on-board temperature sensors: an environment temperature
                                        sensor and a motor temperature sensor. For specifications,
                                        ￼Table ￼.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">The environment
                                        temperature sensor allows for ADI OtoSense™ SMS to take
                                        ambient operating conditions, such as sunlight exposure,
                                        into account when assessing a motor’s temperature
                                        status.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
