                                                  <fo:table-cell start-indent="0" end-indent="0" border-bottom-color="rgb(0 , 0 , 0)" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-width="1px" border-right-color="rgb(0 , 0 , 0)" border-right-style="solid" border-right-width="1px" padding-bottom="0.3em" padding-left="0.3em" padding-right="0.3em" padding-top="0.3em" display-align="before"><fo:block>hours</fo:block></fo:table-cell>
                                                  <fo:table-cell start-indent="0" end-indent="0" border-bottom-color="rgb(0 , 0 , 0)" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-width="1px" padding-bottom="0.3em" padding-left="0.3em" padding-right="0.3em" padding-top="0.3em" display-align="before"><fo:block>Approximation of the motor running time</fo:block></fo:table-cell>
                                                  </fo:table-row>
                                                  <fo:table-row display-align="center">
                                                  <fo:table-cell start-indent="0" end-indent="0" border-right-color="rgb(0 , 0 , 0)" border-right-style="solid" border-right-width="1px" padding-bottom="0.3em" padding-left="0.3em" padding-right="0.3em" padding-top="0.3em" display-align="before"><fo:block>
                                                  <fo:block-container background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0.5em" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em" max-height="600px" chfox:overflow-wrap="break-word" hyphenate="false" break-line-at-hyphens="avoid" role="Code" space-after.conditionality="retain" space-before.conditionality="retain" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="4px" padding-right="4px" padding-top="2px" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" white-space-treatment="preserve" wrap-option="wrap"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:block><fo:block-container background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" font-size="0.8em" padding-bottom="0" padding-left="0" margin-left="0" padding-right="0" margin-right="0" padding-top="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">running</fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:block></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                                  </fo:block></fo:table-cell>
                                                  <fo:table-cell start-indent="0" end-indent="0" border-right-color="rgb(0 , 0 , 0)" border-right-style="solid" border-right-width="1px" padding-bottom="0.3em" padding-left="0.3em" padding-right="0.3em" padding-top="0.3em" display-align="before"><fo:block>Integer flag</fo:block></fo:table-cell>
                                                  <fo:table-cell start-indent="0" end-indent="0" padding-bottom="0.3em" padding-left="0.3em" padding-right="0.3em" padding-top="0.3em" display-align="before"><fo:block>Running flag 1 if running 0 if not running When
                                                  the motor is rotating at a very low speed, less
                                                  than 25% of its rated speed (rated RPM), the
                                                  analytics may interpret the motor as stopped.
                                                  <fo:block-container background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0.5em" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em" max-height="600px" chfox:overflow-wrap="break-word" hyphenate="false" break-line-at-hyphens="avoid" role="Code" space-after.conditionality="retain" space-before.conditionality="retain" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="4px" padding-right="4px" padding-top="2px" linefeed-treatment="preserve" white-space-collapse="false" white-space-treatment="preserve" wrap-option="wrap"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:block><fo:block-container background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" font-size="0.8em" padding-bottom="0" padding-left="0" margin-left="0" padding-right="0" margin-right="0" padding-top="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">running is used to calculate the Number of Starts in a time range.</fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:block><fo:block><fo:block-container background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" font-size="0.8em" padding-bottom="0" padding-left="0" margin-left="0" padding-right="0" margin-right="0" padding-top="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">  Chronologically sort the performance records in the time range and count the number of times _running_ transitions from '0' to '1'. This approximates the number of times the motor started in the specified time range.</fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:block></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                                  </fo:block></fo:table-cell>
                                                  </fo:table-row>
                                                  </fo:table-body></fo:table></fo:table-and-caption>
                                            </fo:block>
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">For more
                                                information on API refer to the ADI OtoSense™ SMS
                                                REST API.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                </fo:block>
                                <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_114" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="conditions">
                                    <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H3" id="ariaid-title93"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d549e13330"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d549e13334"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d549e13338"/><fo:inline>conditions</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">This section
                                            describes the parameters used to assess the condition of
                                            a motor component.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em" role="Sect"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">This
                                                section describes the parameters used to assess the
                                                condition of a motor component.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Each
                                                parameter in the following table represents the
                                                Fault Score Index (FSI) of the corresponding motor
                                                component condition. These predicted health
                                                indicators for motor components are generated each
                                                time the analytics processes data samples received
                                                from a running motor. The values are between zero
                                                and ten:</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                            <fo:list-block relative-align="baseline" provisional-label-separation="3pt" provisional-distance-between-starts="40px" space-after="1.33em" space-before="1.33em" id="unique_114_Connect_42_ul_10211554" chfox:nd-id="ul_10211554">
                                                <fo:list-item><fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()"><fo:block text-align="end">• </fo:block></fo:list-item-label><fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()"><fo:block>A
                                                  value of 10 corresponds to a perfect state for the
                                                  component.</fo:block></fo:list-item-body></fo:list-item>
                                                <fo:list-item><fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()"><fo:block text-align="end">• </fo:block></fo:list-item-label><fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()"><fo:block>A
                                                  value of 0 corresponds to a catastrophic state for
                                                  the component.</fo:block></fo:list-item-body></fo:list-item>
                                            </fo:list-block>
                                        </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block>
